<title>FRANCE: GAN renews CIC unit ties.</title>
<headline>GAN renews CIC unit ties.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>French state-controlled insurer GAN has signed new 10-year exlusivity agreements with its CIC banking unit on the distribution of GAN insurance products, GAN chairman Jean-Jacques Bonnaud said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The government has launched a tender for the privatization of the CIC banking group, with 67 percent of CIC on offer.</p>
<p>&quot;We have signed exclusivity contracts on the entire range of life and non-life insurance products for a period of 10 year,&quot; he told reporters.</p>
<p>The conditions tied to the CIC tender note that suitors should allow for continuation of the links between CIC and GAN.</p>
<p>Bonnaud said the deal with CIC allowed for penalties if the bank did not respect the exclusivity principle.</p>
</text>
